## NixOS rebuilds and CI (2026-10-18)

**NixOS: deploy only the pushed branch head, so every agent's committed change ships.** Push first;
`get` deploys `main` (`scripts/deploy`), vps-primary `master` promoted to `deploy-vps-primary`; never
a local, side-branch or older commit. A deploy in flight: wait, redeploy the new head, check the
deployed revision. Heavy builds and `nix flake update` run on Forgejo CI, not on vps-primary.

**Heavy jobs run in CI, not on the Mac: GitHub runners for GitHub-sourced repos (`ci/base` + `ci/run/**`,
`scripts/github-*` wrappers); Forgejo/Hyades CI for MIT/SIPB and private work that needs it** (`forgejo-ci`
skill, item 6; djbclark 2026-10-19).

## Reply formatting — number every list

**Every bulleted list in a reply to djbclark uses numbers or letters, never plain `-`/`*` bullets**
(tables are fine). With more than one list, never restart at 1: `1.1`/`2.1` or `1a`/`2b`. Label each
item once: never a `1.` list marker plus a `1.1` label (2026-10-14). Every URL is a markdown link
`[label](url)`; anything to click, copy or paste goes in prose before a question card, which Paseo
renders unselectable and unlinkified (getpaseo/paseo#3164; 2026-10-19).

## Other agent CLIs, and delegating to them

Binary names differ from provider ids (antigravity → `agy`, zai → `zcode`, opencode-go → `opencode`,
cursor → `cursor-agent`; table: `memory/reference_agent_rules_code_discovery_and_cli_table.md`);
gemini is deprecated, not installed. Every agent but muse speaks ACP (`acp-run --list`).

**Delegation route, in order:** (1) **`acp-run <agent> -C <dir> -p '<prompt>' --model <m>`**
(`~/.local/bin/acp-run`; **always `--model`**, zcode too since 2026-10-15; `--effort`/`--context`
too; check its `applied:` line; yolo-only since 2026-10-14, `--perm deny` for review-only slices; exit
0 is not success, verify tests/diff); (2) Orca `worker-start`; (3) a Herdr pane; (4) non-ACP CLIs:
their own headless recipe. **copilot is the only reserve: floor 60% left, one small GitHub slice**;
grok is an ordinary pool (2026-10-18; `acp-run grok --model grok-4.7`). **hermes is never a delegation target. Never an all-vendor
fan-out**: `route_agent.py plan` picks vendor × model × effort per slice. **cline (uninstalled
2026-10-17) never without djbclark's explicit approval for that run** (refused unless
`ACP_OPERATOR_APPROVED=cline`). **The Claude API credits (`omp`, 2026-10-19) are a normal tier,
used with discernment: `api-only` work first, else code/bulk slices via `acp-run omp --model anthropic/claude-...`,
never left unspent** (`djbclark-ade/skills/model-routing/SKILL.md`).

**Routing policy (2026-10-15): minimise cost, maximise code quality.** Frontier models are scarce:
judgment is Opus `high`; codex `gpt-6-astra` and Fable `high` only for work that really needs them
(codex one slice in flight, Fable `xhigh` almost never); everyday work on other pools at the minimum
spec. **claude codes on Sonnet 5.5, never Fable**; quota never buys a pool more than 10 rank steps
below the best into code/judgment. Claude tiers: Haiku lookups, Sonnet executes, Opus plans, reviews
and advises, Fable frontier; climb on evidence. **`acp-dispatch` needs `--kind`, refuses an ineligible
pool, and runs `frontier` as an advisor unless `ACP_OPERATOR_APPROVED=frontier-exec`; cheapest eligible
tier first.** One copy: `skills/model-routing/SKILL.md` *Routing policy* (numbers:
`djbclark-ade/config/routing.toml`).

