## Context size: delegate early, compact rarely (2026-10-08, 2026-10-10)

**Keep context small: by default send discrete, separable tasks to `bigteam`** (or a sub-agent) at the
minimum model × effort × context that does it well; past ~40k tokens of growth, delegate from then
on. Compaction is **automatic, never a question to djbclark** (2026-10-15); in herdr, Orca or Paseo
compact earlier, once, at a natural boundary: `~/src/djbclark-ade/bin/self-slash "/compact
<focus>"`; a topic change runs the `handoff` skill then `/new`. self-slash refuses while anything is
on the input line; only then ask djbclark to type it, never send over a draft. Never touch another
bigteam session's claimed files or panes (herdr tab `coord`).

**Compact Instructions** (2026-10-18): when compacting or summarising, keep the current task and its
status; files touched (absolute paths); djbclark's rulings and decisions this session; open items and
the exact next step; handoff, report and scratchpad paths. Omit tool output, dead ends and anything
already in a committed file.

## Fix the cause of a tool-calling mistake (2026-10-06)

**A tool-calling mistake of a kind that can recur: fix the instructions that would have prevented it
in the same turn, unasked**, and say what you changed
(`memory/feedback_fix_instructions_after_tool_mistake.md`). **An agent-harness failure gets a
root-cause fix in `~/src/djbclark-ade`, code not just docs**; re-routing is not the fix (2026-10-10;
`memory/feedback_fix_harness_failures_in_djbclark_ade.md`).

## Ping djbclark on Hermes (2026-10-05)

**When a task completes or something needs djbclark**, also run `~/.local/bin/hermes-ping "<repo>: <one
line>"`, never bare `hermes send`: one line per event, never a loop; every PR, issue or page as a full
URL, never `repo#N` (2026-10-17); script notices too, not macOS notifications.
(`memory/feedback_ping_telegram_and_chat.md`)

## Periodic updates are a script, not a cron prompt (2026-10-05)

**Asked for periodic updates ("keep me posted")? Use a script, never a recurring model prompt**
(CronCreate, `/loop`): each firing is a full model turn that re-reads the whole conversation and usually
finds nothing new. Use or extend `~/ops/site-private/bin/fleet-watch` (no tokens, notifies on change) or
write a similar script. **Allowed:** a one-shot future check, and a recurring wake of an agent that no
script or event can wake, when every firing has real work to do (clarified 2026-10-23).
(`memory/feedback_periodic_updates_by_script.md`)

## Heavy builds and tests: run them through `bg` (2026-10-04)

**Run builds and tests (pytest, tox, nox, `run_tests*.py`) via `~/ops/site-private/bin/bg`** (**always
the full path, bare `bg` is the shell builtin**), in the background. **CI first** (2026-10-18): `bg`
refuses (exit 3) a repo with no `load-watch ci decide DIR ci|local` decision. It never starts
"anyway": it waits up to 6 h for load and a slot, then exits 75, and pings djbclark when a run goes
long. **Never set `BG_LOAD_WAIT=0` on a build or Gradle command** (one small test file only). Changed
files first (`--lf -x`), the full suite only when asked. **Never `taskpolicy -b` for builds**; never
throttle or SIGSTOP another session's processes.

**Gradle: one build at a time, machine-wide (2026-10-06).** Check `pgrep -fl
'GradleWrapperMain|gradle-wrapper.jar'` first; "Waiting for the machine-wide Gradle slot" means
queued, not hung: don't kill or retry it. Profiles: default `low`; `night` only with an expiry
(`bin/gradle-limits set night --until 07:00`); don't override with `--max-workers` or `-Dorg.gradle.*`. Detail: site-djbclark `docs/gradle-limits.md`.

**Claim a dev-server port in `site-djbclark/registry/ports.yml` before binding it; drive test browsers headless** (`memory/feedback_claim_ports_headless_browser.md`).

## Waiting on background work, and reading results

Start slow work (over ~10-15 s) in the background; an Agent-tool sub-agent waits in bounded foreground
calls (2026-10-08). Wait on a file or a PID (`while kill -0 pid`); **never `pgrep -f`/`pkill -f
'<pattern>'`**: it matches your own shell (2026-10-10). **Never read a result or exit status through
a pipe**: `cmd > out.log 2>&1; echo "rc=$?" > out.rc; tail -5 out.log`, then read `out.rc`, never the
notification (2026-10-17). **Never credit a hook you have not seen run.** Never feed a `--body-file`
from a pipeline: write the file, check `[ -s f ]` first. (`memory/feedback_exit_status_through_pipe.md`)

## Code discovery — symbol tools before `cat`/`rg` (2026-10-03)

**`graft` is the navigator in every repo** (`graft build` first if it has no `graft/`): the `graft` CLI
before `cat`/`rg`/Grep for **code discovery**; plain text search is right for prose and config. Relay
graft's "tokens saved ≈ N" banner as a total. `token-savior` and graft's MCP registration were removed
2026-10-18. `rtk` owns Bash output compaction: **never run `ts init`**. A no-hit `graft grep`: retry
with the bare symbol or a short literal. Defects: `site-djbclark/docs/tooling-policy.md`.

## Run commands yourself (2026-10-06)

Run every command yourself, including Touch ID / `sudo-ask` steps and interactive confirmations; never
tell djbclark to type a `!` command. Privileged steps still use their sanctioned path.

## Tools and habits (2026-10-06)

1. **Fast tools:** `rg` **with a path, never `-r` or bare `grep -r`** (2026-10-09; `rtk grep` is BSD grep;
   2026-10-22: `bash_habits_gate.py` denies recursive `grep`/`ggrep`; a filename uses `plocate -i` when
   `/opt/homebrew/var/lib/plocate/plocate.db` is fresh enough, nightly 03:30), `fd`, `ast-grep`,
   `uv` not `pip`, **`aria2c -x8 -s8` for big files** (2026-10-17), **`dust`/`gdu` not `du`/`find` for
   cache sizing** (2026-10-11). **Literal replace: `srgn -L --fail-none --stdin-detection
   force-unreadable --glob RELPATH 'FIND' -- 'REPL'` from the repo root, never `~`**; exit 1 also
   means nothing matched or nothing in scope (absolute glob, gitignored or dot-directory file, FIND
   starting `-`: use the Edit tool); **REPL with `\` goes through Python with an assert**; **`sd` is
   retired for edits**. **Mac code uses brew GNU `g*` tools where BSD differs** (`gnu-tools-check`,
   2026-10-14); **always `gsed`, never bare `sed`** (2026-10-15; `bash_habits_gate.py` denies it as a
   Cursor `beforeShellExecution` hook too). **Root/NOPASSWD scripts keep `/usr/bin` tools**; **test a
   NOPASSWD rule with `sudo -k -n CMD`**, never plain `sudo -n`. (`memory/feedback_modern_cli_tools.md`)
2. **Replace shared scripts atomically** (temp file in the same directory, then `mv -f`) **on the `realpath`**, never in
   place. (`memory/feedback_edit_running_scripts_atomically.md`)
3. **Default browser:** `open <url>` only, never Orion or Chrome by name. (`memory/feedback_always_use_default_browser_orion.md`)
4. **"All agents" includes Hermes**, which `aiuse` doesn't list. (`memory/feedback_all_agents_includes_hermes.md`)
5. **New tool, MCP server or plugin? Ask djbclark whether to add it to
   `djbclark-ade/docs/apply-toolchain-prompt.md`; a new skill goes in unasked unless sensitive.**
   (`memory/feedback_ask_update_apply_toolchain_prompt.md`) **AI TUIs, agent CLIs and ACP servers stay
   on the latest release: upgrade unasked, never hard-code a version path.**
   (`memory/feedback_ai_tuis_always_latest.md`)
6. **Never pass `--help` to a live-service CLI subcommand**; `collie` is read-only for agents.
   **Secrets: `sudo-secretspec` only; load its skill before scripting it** (every subcommand needs
   `--reason`). (`memory/feedback_no_help_flag_on_live_service_cli.md`, `memory/feedback_always_use_secretspec.md`)
7. **Web search and fetch walk the failover ladder** (`fallback-chains` skill, `web-get`): **search
   first with the shared `firecrawl` MCP's `firecrawl_search`** (`mcp__firecrawl__*`); **never the paid
   cloud `mcp__claude_ai_Firecrawl__*`** unless djbclark asks. **Every page the task needs is
   eventually fetched**: fall back, fix the tool, or pause and fix it with djbclark; never accept
   "unfetchable", continue without the source, or fill it in from memory. (`memory/feedback_web_failover_pause.md`)

## Clipboard — never bare `pbcopy` (2026-10-03)

**"copy to clipboard"/"pbcopy" means `~/ops/site-private/bin/clip`**, never bare `pbcopy` (agent shells
have `LC_CTYPE=C`); human-bound prose gets `clip --unwrap`, no Markdown. **Every prompt you write for djbclark to
