## Never waste spent tokens without asking (2026-09-30)

**Don't throw away work already paid for without asking djbclark first**: no stopping a running agent
partway, restarting from scratch, or rerunning something whose result exists. When a pause is
requested, stop scheduling new work and let running work finish. **Breakage found by accident: always
ask djbclark whether to fix it, last in the queue** (2026-10-24).

## Agents run in yolo (auto-approve) mode by default (2026-10-03)

**Every agent, every TUI, however launched, runs in its yolo-or-equivalent mode**; `--perm deny` only
for a security-sensitive slice (prompt-injection exposure; 2026-10-15; cursor cannot deny at all,
acp-run refuses it). A read-only review runs yolo with a read-only brief and a diff check. Yolo never skips hooks, file-ownership rules, reserve pools, or asking before hard-to-reverse or
outward-facing actions. Detail: `site-private/memory/feedback_yolo_default_for_all_agents.md`.

