At session start in a git repo, read its Tier 1 pointer (`~/.local/state/handoffs/`), compare
`head_sha` to `HEAD`, and state a resume plan before acting. Only the workspace-owning session writes
it. Protocol: `~/src/djbclark-ade/skills/session-handoff/SKILL.md`.

## Three-way memory/docs policy (start at each repo's AGENTS.md)

No single canonical copy — read all three: `stayturgid/AGENTS.md`, `site-djbclark/AGENTS.md`,
`site-private/AGENTS.md`.

## Research outward first (2026-10-05)

**About to spend significant tokens on something a web search might answer? Search first** (how a
tool, library, protocol or error behaves, other projects' source and issue trackers included), before
trial and error or rounds of local grepping. Then verify locally.
